WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.620
Hi! I'm Briana from 
freeCodeCamp.

00:00:02.980 --> 00:00:05.480
Today we are going to be 
talking about Git and GitHub:

00:00:05.480 --> 00:00:07.260
how you use them, 
when you use them,

00:00:07.260 --> 00:00:09.480
and some of the differences 
between the two.

00:00:09.740 --> 00:00:11.820
To start off, 
let's talk about Git.

00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:14.420
Git is a 
version control software,

00:00:14.420 --> 00:00:15.740
which means 
while you're coding

00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:18.480
you can save each little time 
you make a change.

00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:19.860
So if you 
make a mistake,

00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:21.700
you want to 
undo something,

00:00:21.700 --> 00:00:22.740
or you just want 
to look back

00:00:22.740 --> 00:00:23.880
and see how 
it was before,

00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:25.120
you can do 
that with Git.

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:27.440
Git is also 
open source.

00:00:27.440 --> 00:00:29.420
You can find 
Git to download

00:00:29.420 --> 00:00:31.740
at http://git-scm.com

00:00:31.740 --> 00:00:33.640
they also have 
great resources

00:00:33.640 --> 00:00:35.040
for documentation.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:37.520
Now let's talk 
about GitHub.

00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:39.460
You've probably been 
on GitHub before

00:00:39.460 --> 00:00:41.120
for some 
freeCodeCamp things,

00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:43.500
noticed it there, 
you probably even have an account.

00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:45.960
GitHub is a 
collaboration website

00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:48.580
that interacts with Git 
and works with it

00:00:48.580 --> 00:00:50.160
on the projects 
that you work on

00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:51.920
in your 
version control.

00:00:52.600 --> 00:00:54.460
It's hard to tell 
where the line is

00:00:54.460 --> 00:00:56.720
between what's Git 
and what's GitHub -

00:00:57.220 --> 00:00:58.900
that's okay, 
you don't have to know.

00:00:59.220 --> 00:01:00.560
What you need 
to remember is

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:03.840
you'll use GitHub 
to interact with Git.

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:05.660
You'll use it 
to collaborate

00:01:05.660 --> 00:01:09.580
with your peers on projects
using version control.

